[32m+[m[32m## Objectives and feature ownership[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach developer owns the interface, validation, server operations, data changes, and tests for their two modules.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Owner | Module | Demonstration outcome |[m
[32m+[m[32m| --- | --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Developer 1 — blue | Civic Reporting | Submit category, description, optional photo, and GPS/manual location; receive a tracking ID; view history; let staff update status. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Developer 1 — blue | Emergency Hotlines and Alerts | Browse PNP, BFP, hospital, and MDRRMO categories; call only independently verified numbers. Alerts are optional. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Developer 2 — green | Online LGU Services | Submit a reusable service form, receive a reference, view history, and let staff review/update status. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Developer 2 — green | Municipal Projects and Services | Browse offices, contacts, services, and upcoming/ongoing/completed projects. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Developer 3 — pink | Worker Census and Social Profiling | Manage synthetic worker records behind staff access; import a small sample; show aggregates. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Developer 3 — pink | Job Matching | Browse/filter jobs and let authorized staff match a census worker using occupation, skills, and barangay. |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mShared objectives are ownership-based access, persistent records, usable mobile forms, and a repeatable demonstration. Matching reuses census data without exposing individual socioeconomic records.[m
[32m+[m
